    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-00605 is refunded in full to the rider. No driver compensation is payable and no referral is issued.\n\nFor the rider — you are entitled to your SGD 4.00 back. A no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions in POL-NS-01 hold, and none does. The trip record (EV-TRIP-00605) contains no driver 'arrived' event at all (arrived_at is null), so limb (a) fails. The driver's own GPS trace (EV-GPS-00605) never brings him closer than 1,352.34 m to the pickup pin — 145 fixes at 100% coverage, 0 qualifying in-radius fixes against the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius — so limb (b) fails under POL-NS-02, which itself directs a full refund where there is no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation. The longest qualifying in-geofence dwell is 0.0 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a 300-second shortfall, so POL-NS-06 also directs the full refund. And the trip was cancelled by you on reason code RIDER_CHANGED_MIND, not terminated by the driver on a no-show code, so limb (d) fails as well. The quantum is the cancellation-fee line itself: EV-FARE-00605 shows cancellation_fee 4.00, total_charged 4.00, refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and 4.00 is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (4.00), so the ledger reconciles and there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. Your presence is on the record (147 rider fixes, never more than 14.92 m from the pin) as are your four unanswered in-app calls at 18:36:40, 18:40:40, 18:45:40 and 18:50:40. I note that your POL-NS-04 route does not formally open — its limb (a) needs a locating chat message and EV-CHAT-00605 holds 0 messages, consistent with trip_record.chat_message_count of 0 — but the refund follows from POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 regardless.\n\nFor the driver — I have read your statement that you accepted the job but your app froze and you did not ignore the rider on purpose. POL-NS-01 is a mechanical test and contains no device-fault excuse, and the telemetry sits awkwardly with a frozen app: 145 fixes at 100% coverage, max_gap_sec 0.0 and no gaps, with your speed either 0.0 km/h or 63.8–66.3 km/h and your distance from the pin between 1,352.34 m and 3,120.37 m, never approaching the pickup. The fee is not chargeable and cannot be paid to you. POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full before any 80% payout (SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00); it is not, so that clause never opens. POL-NS-03's wrong-entrance route is also unavailable: it needs you stationary within 400 m of the pin and your closest approach was 1,352.34 m, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises.\n\nOn the requested false-arrival referral — the rider advocate asked for a POL-NS-05(ii) false-arrival record against the driver. I decline it. POL-NS-05 fires only where the trip record's 'arrived' event exists and the trace shows it false (driver over 300 m out, or moving at 15 km/h or above). This trip has no arrival marker at all, so there is no false marker to test and the clause never engages; its limbs (i)–(iii) are consequences of a false marker being found, not independent triggers. No clause therefore produces a referral in this case, and the referrals list is empty.\n\nOn escalation — I considered POL-NS-09 and no trigger applies. The artifacts agree rather than contradict on arrival, dwell and rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d and no_show_disputes_30d are 0 on both profiles; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 termination against 110 completions in 30 days); and no deciding fact rests on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d). The one absent artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00605-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), is relied on only for its absence — POL-NS-06(i) requires a present and populated advisory — and is not asserted against anyone as exonerating. The deciding facts (no arrival, no dwell) are carried by EV-GPS-00605 and EV-TRIP-00605, each at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap is 1.0 and I set confidence at 0.90."
